			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				136,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance Element submodule — registry-backed vscode.tests namespace shim\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to 9b3109db, replacing the stock inline no-op stub for `vscode.tests` in Cocoon's EnsureVscodeAPI.ts with a dynamically-imported, registry-backed TestsNamespace factory.\n\nEach TestController now owns a `Map`-backed `TestItemCollection` with working add/delete/get/replace/forEach, a profile registry for `createRunProfile`, and a `TestRun` state machine tracking the full queued/started/skipped/failed/errored/passed lifecycle. Re-registering a controller with the same id returns the existing instance, softening VS Code's duplicate-id throw for dev-reload double-calls.\n\nExtensions like vitest, mocha-explorer, and rust-analyzer that consume `vscode.tests` now maintain correct internal state instead of silently dropping `controller.items.add(item)` calls against the old stub.",
			"SHA": "5e47a39363c8654206b10bdfb8111ef5c8925a66"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T08:12:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				136,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance Element submodule — diff info, view column, terminal state bridge, and command broadcast flag\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to 0de33710, integrating the Mountain-to-Cocoon notification relay for three additional extension API surfaces plus the TierCommandEventBroadcast feature flag.\n\nSky adds three snapshot-style bridge subscriptions guarded with try/catch: diff editor onDidUpdateDiff line-changes relayed as sky:editor:diffInformationChanged, per-group onDidMoveEditor relayed as sky:editor:viewColumnChanged, and OSC 633 B terminal interaction detection relayed via localPty:setInteracted.\n\nMountain fans three new IPC notifications through WindServiceHandlers — $acceptTextEditorDiffInformationChanged, $acceptTextEditorViewColumnChanged, and $acceptTerminalStateChanged — and introduces TierCommandEventBroadcast (default Off) which dual-emits $acceptCommandExecuted over Vine after gRPC Command.Execute from Cocoon, ensuring onDidExecuteCommand fires for non-locally-registered extension host commands.\n\nCocoon registers four Notification/Handler.ts cases: $activateByEvent defers to ExtensionHostHandler via setImmediate so extension activation actually runs; $acceptTextEditorDiffInformationChanged emits didChangeTextEditorDiffInformation keyed on modifiedUri; $acceptTextEditorViewColumnChanged fires didChangeTextEditorViewColumn with URI and viewColumn matching VS Code's event shape; $acceptTerminalStateChanged updates the cached terminal's isInteractedWith flag and emits didChangeTerminalState. The Auth namespace also subscribes to each AuthenticationProvider.onDidChangeSessions on registration with proper disposal on provider unregister to prevent listener leaks.\n\nThe accompanying Cargo.toml bumps http, log, reqwest, rhai, and all OXC dependencies to their latest patch/minor versions. turbo.json adds TierCommandEventBroadcast to the compile-time feature flag pipeline alongside the existing TierSearch, TierStorage, TierTasks, and TierTelemetry flags.\n\nExtensions consuming didChangeTextEditorDiffInformation, didChangeTextEditorViewColumn, didChangeTerminalState, and onDidExecuteCommand now receive live workbench signals through the complete Mountain-to-Cocoon bridge.",
			"SHA": "72c78c72671b51b5fca37f5a36df5b7bb34d1073"
		},
