				136,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance Element submodule — terminal shell execution event relay\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to d43cffe1, integrating the end-to-end bridge for VS Code terminal shell execution lifecycle events across Cocoon, Mountain, and Sky.\n\nSky parses OSC 633 sequences beyond the existing cwd handler — adding OscEndPattern (;D[;<exitCode>]) and OscCmdLinePattern (;E;<commandLine>) regex parsers plus a per-terminal InflightExecution Map. On OSC 633;C (output begins), Sky fires `localPty:shellExecutionStart` via Mountain IPC; on ;D (command finished), it fires `localPty:shellExecutionEnd` with exitCode, clearing the cached commandLine for the next execution.\n\nMountain adds two WindServiceHandlers for `localPty:shellExecutionStart` and `localPty:shellExecutionEnd`, fanning the former as `$acceptTerminalShellExecutionStart` to Cocoon and the latter as two Vine notifications: `$acceptTerminalShellExecutionEnd` and a derived `$acceptExecutedTerminalCommand` so extension subscribers observe executed commands without an additional Sky-side detection pass.\n\nCocoon registers three Notification/Handler.ts cases — `$acceptTerminalShellExecutionStart`, `$acceptTerminalShellExecutionEnd`, and `$acceptExecutedTerminalCommand` — each resolving the matching terminal from the `__terminals` context cache and assembling the VS Code event shape with the required terminal, shellIntegration, and execution sub-objects including the `{ value, isTrusted }` commandLine contract.\n\nExtension subscribers hooked via `window.didStartTerminalShellExecution`, `window.didEndTerminalShellExecution`, and `window.didExecuteTerminalCommand` now receive live notifications from OSC 633 sequence parsing in the Sky terminal layer.",
			"SHA": "b1968f3dc1b03822af26982256b33f98cad3ac55"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T22:10:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				136,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodule — bridged editor state, diagnostics, theme, and breakpoint event pipeline\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to c3783083, integrating Cocoon notification handlers and Mountain-to-Cocoon fan-out for six extension API surfaces that were previously renderer-only.\n\nCocoon adds Notification/Handler.ts cases for $acceptDiagnosticsChanged, $acceptVisibleEditorsChanged, $acceptTabsChanged, $acceptVisibleRangesChanged, $acceptTextEditorOptionsChanged, and $acceptActiveColorTheme — each pumping the Mountain notification through the matching Emitter channel. The $acceptTabsChanged handler caches tab-group snapshots on __tabGroups so synchronous window.tabGroups.all getters reflect current state.\n\nMountain fans five notification types back to Cocoon: $acceptActiveColorTheme in ThemesSet.rs on theme switch, $acceptVisibleEditorsChanged/$acceptTabsChanged/$acceptVisibleRangesChanged/$acceptTextEditorOptionsChanged in WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs forwarding Sky payloads, $acceptDiagnosticsChanged in Diagnostics.rs after Set/Clear calls, and $onDidChangeBreakpoints in DebugLifecycle.rs for breakpoint mutations.\n\nSky bridges four Monaco/workbench event streams through the IPC layer: onDidScrollChange (debounced to ~16 fps) emits visible ranges, onDidChangeConfiguration emits options changes, onDidVisibleEditorsChange emits the URI list of visible editors, and onDidChangeActiveGroup/onDidAddGroup/onDidRemoveGroup emit tab-group snapshots. All IPC calls are wrapped in try/catch so render failures never interrupt the UI pipeline.\n\nVS Code API subscribers inside Cocoon — languages.onDidChangeDiagnostics, window.onDidChangeVisibleTextEditors, window.tabGroups.onDidChangeTabs, window.onDidChangeTextEditorVisibleRanges, window.onDidChangeTextEditorOptions, window.onDidChangeActiveColorTheme, and debug.onDidChangeBreakpoints — now fire correctly for all extensions.",
			"SHA": "4f239fbb7f63ad88216d43f491062f299efeba4d"
		}
	],
